WEBVTT

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:33.280
Shirou!

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.240
Shirou!

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.240
It's starting to rain!

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:44.460
Uh-oh, I've got the laundry hanging outside.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.090
Where's Saber?

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.420
Out shopping!

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:59.890
<i>Days like these remind me...</i>

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.690
<i>...of those nostalgic days gone by.</i>

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.440
Shirou!

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.960
Here! Here! Here! Here!

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.790
Hey, dummy!

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:28.960
Don't throw them!

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.340
Okay!

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.640
They got a little damp.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.650
Oh, this is no big deal at all!

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:53.490
<i>Pierce them with a bamboo skewer,
and if there's any translucent juice,</i>

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:56.240
<i>finish them off by browning them, and you're done!</i>

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:00.490
<i>This week's "Show Me How to Make Dinner"
was all about making homemade—</i>

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.630
You going somewhere?

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.840
Shopping for dinner.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:16.840
Is that right?

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.180
Then maybe I'll go with you.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.390
To do what?

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.020
Get snacks and stuff!

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.620
<i>MOUNT MIYAMA SHOPPING TOWN</i>

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:36.860
First the ground beef, then the onions...

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.330
You're in my way!

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:45.290
Hey, fish shop guy!

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.290
Sell us some fish cheap!

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.040
Forget that, let's go!

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.060
Show me.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.110
Okay.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:17.820
Today's menu is harder than
anything you've made before, right?

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:20.780
I wonder if you can pull it off!

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.410
Sure I can!

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.160
I think.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:28.750
Bean paste cakes!

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.830
That'll ruin your appetite for dinner!

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.630
Shirou! Shirou!

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:40.840
Did something make you sad?

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:43.640
It's the onions making my eyes sting!

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:47.470
Okay, when you're ready, I'll read this aloud to you.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:54.940
First...

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:59.190
Take half of the finely chopped
onions, and saute them on low heat.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.410
When they're fully coated with oil, add a dash of salt.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:07.490
And once they're caramelized, cool them off.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.750
And leave the rest of the onions raw.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.380
Place the chilled ground beef
and a dash of salt in a bowl.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.510
Mix it well until it's slightly sticky.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:26.600
As quickly as possible...

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.810
When you've mixed the meat thoroughly,

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:35.150
add bread crumbs, egg, nutmeg, pepper...

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.230
The raw onions...

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:41.070
Add the onions you sauteed earlier,

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:43.950
and mix them in.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:52.160
Drop the meat from one hand
to another to remove the air...

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.500
...and shape them into patties around 1.5 cm thick.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.090
When you've shaped them to your liking...

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.970
...leave them in the refrigerator for 30 minutes or so.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:04.840
While I'm waiting,

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:08.220
I'm going to make powdery
potatoes and sauteed green beans.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.430
So it's not just hamburgers!

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.900
Warm up the frying pan and grill them on medium heat.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:23.900
Once a crust forms, grill them
for three minutes on low heat.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:29.120
When the sides turn white, flip
them over and grill them some more.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:34.250
Turn off the heat, cover them and
leave them for two or three minutes.

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:38.380
Turn on the heat again and grill for two minutes or so.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:40.920
Poke the patties with a bamboo skewer.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:45.340
If you see translucent juice, it's a sign that it's done.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.350
Lastly, cook on high heat for 15 seconds or so.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.060
Once the patties are browned...

00:05:58.110 --> 00:05:59.730
Done!

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:04.360
Wow, I can't believe it's the first time you made them!

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:07.450
You sure have a flair for cooking, Shirou!

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.740
Yeah, never mind that. Let's get these to the table.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:11.950
Roger that!

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:19.880
Something smells delicious.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:22.460
Hey, time to eat...

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:24.720
Grandpa!

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:33.310
Did you two make these?

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.430
No, it was Shirou!

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.400
I helped out just a tiny bit!

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:42.730
You like hamburgers, don't you, Grandpa?

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:51.830
All right, shall we partake, then?

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:55.120
Thank you for the meal!

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:17.480
This is good.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:20.230
You're something else, Shirou.

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:22.940
I can't believe you can already cook this well.

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:27.650
No, I've got a long way to go.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:31.660
I bet you've had way better food overseas.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.240
Well,

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:37.580
I can't forget the hamburgers I had in Germany.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:40.000
What were they like?

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.250
Thicker than what we'd eat in Japan,

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.050
and it was quite filling.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:49.170
Okay, then, next time I'm gonna make
some tastier than the ones in Germany.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:52.180
That's certainly ambitious of you.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:53.930
Yep, yep.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:57.680
Watching over your progress
is another one of my missions!

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:01.520
Seriously, I'm gonna have to keep coming over, huh?

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:04.060
But you always show up for no reason anyway.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:08.690
But Mr. Kiritsugu, you sure have been all over the world!

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:11.110
Will you be traveling again soon?

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:14.700
I don't know.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:19.750
But I'd hate to miss out on Shirou's
cooking if I did have to leave.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:22.750
Well, then...

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:25.130
Just stay here forever!

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:31.380
And I'll get even better.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:37.560
That goes for those hamburgers you love so much, too!

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:42.440
So please...

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:45.110
Forever...

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:47.110
Forever...

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:56.370
You should stay here forever.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:07.340
I see.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:15.010
Well...

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.350
I can't wait to see your progress.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:24.650
Shirou!

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:27.190
Give me another hamburger please!

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:31.360
You sure aren't shy, Fuji-nee.

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:35.990
A healthy appetite is a good thing, Shirou.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.460
I'm telling you, it was pouring!

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:46.500
It was such a hassle bringing the laundry in!

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:48.790
Yes, that was quite a downpour.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:53.340
Did you get caught in the rain
when you were shopping, Saber?

00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:56.220
I had an umbrella, so I was fine.

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:02.980
Shi...

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:04.230
rou!

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.980
I-Ilya! Did you say you were coming over?

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:13.240
No, I was in the neighborhood, so I thought I'd drop by.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.490
Hamburgs?

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:22.910
Yeah. I used to make these all the time.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:24.370
Wanna join us?

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.500
Thanks for having us!

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.500
Something smells good!

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:32.000
It really does!

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:34.510
Shirou!

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:37.010
I'm starving!

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:40.510
Hurry up!

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:46.020
Really, Taiga, when will you learn to be patient?

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.850
That's harsh!

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:52.020
We're having Shirou's hamburgers today, you know!

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.030
Jeez...

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.320
Sorry to keep you waiting!
